  "answer": "Traditional support lookup tasks in this corpus are natural-language queries to TutorChat: employees ask conversational questions, TutorChat runs semantic search against the KnowledgeHub index, applies role-based permission filtering, and returns grounded, cited answers [NL-002#NL-002-S03]. The validation Golden Dataset also includes \"direct lookup\" queries as one of its query categories [NL-008#NL-008-S08].\n\nStructured BI-style questions, by contrast, are SQL aggregations run against telemetry tables such as `support_tickets` and `customer_satisfaction_log`, e.g. `SELECT category, SUM(ticket_count) ... GROUP BY category`, `SELECT segment, AVG(ticket_count) ... GROUP BY segment`, and SLA/customer-satisfaction queries [NL-029#NL-029-S07].\n\nSo the lookup workflow is conversational, document-chunk-based, and citation-verified, while BI-style questions are programmatic, table-based, and aggregate-oriented.\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
